# AGENTS.md — <your-repo-name> (Codex)

Rules for the AI operator when it's **Codex** (the `AGENTS.md` analog of `CLAUDE.md.template`).
The framework is Claude-first; this is the cheap Codex equivalent. The **rules are identical** —
only the filename and a couple of config locations differ. See `guide/03-governance-rules.md`
for the reasoning and `CLAUDE.md.template` for the fully-annotated version.

> If you run Claude Code, use `CLAUDE.md.template` instead. Running both CLIs? Keep the rule
> *content* in sync between the two files (or generate both from one source via the config
> manager) so the operator behaves the same whichever CLI you use — that's Rule 7 (symmetry)
> applied to your own tooling.

## Repo purpose

<One paragraph — what this repo is, described by ROLE not machine name. Same as the CLAUDE.md
version.>

Nodes (by role): `workstation`, `server`, … (map your real machines to roles once, in the
config manager's data).

**Source of truth:** `<git-host>/<your-repo-name>` (private). Machines are derived; never edit
a node directly.

## Rules (locked — re-read before every commit)

1. **No destructive/material action without explicit approval** — applying config, deleting
   non-backed-up files, creating remote artifacts, bootstrapping a service, any state-mutating
   remote command.
2. **No version-control state change without explicit approval — every time** — `git add`
   included, plus commit/push/reset/rebase and any host mutation (PR/issue/repo). Reads are free.
3. **Secrets never enter version control** — enforced by the ignore files; when in doubt, don't
   stage it.
4. **Back up before you apply.**
5. **Default to symmetry across same-role nodes** — divergence must be unavoidable or
   temporary-with-cleanup.
6. **Production/source defaults unchanged.**
7. **No undocumented deferral** — write deferrals into a plan doc with reason + when.
8. **Status lives in `<registry-file>` + project docs, not memory.**
9. **Before requesting commit approval, list the next steps** that follow the commit + push.
10. **Re-read these rules before every commit.**
11. **Keep the status view in sync in the same commit** as any status/checklist change.
12. *(your own locked rules)*

## Workflow

Edit in the dev clone → (approval) commit + push → on each node pull the prod source → backup →
diff → (approval) apply → verify. Same flow as the Claude version.

## Codex-specific config locations

- **This rules file:** `AGENTS.md` at the repo root (Codex reads it like Claude reads
  `CLAUDE.md`).
- **Model / global config:** `~/.codex/config.toml`.
- **MCP servers:** the `[mcp_servers]` section of `~/.codex/config.toml` — see
  `skeleton/mcp/codex.mcp.toml` (placeholders, no tokens/paths; `guide/10-mcp.md`).
- **Permissions:** Codex's own approval settings — map the framework's presets
  (cautious/standard/trusting, `guide/09-permissions.md`) to Codex's equivalents; the
  invariant holds: never auto-approve pushes, deletes, deploys, or service bootstraps.

## File scope / restricted

Same as the Claude version: docs/registry/rules editable; SSH config/keys, credential dirs, and
anything holding secrets are off-limits without explicit instruction.
